  "model_selection_rationale": "XGBoost shows modestly higher observed fold-mean discrimination (ROC-AUC 0.736 vs 0.725; PR-AUC 0.617 vs 0.609) and a slightly lower Brier score (0.2054 vs 0.2098) compared to RandomForest on repeated-CV fold summaries. These observed differences are small relative to cross-fold variance (SD ~0.06\u20130.08) and do not establish formal statistical significance. Standard cutoff 0.50 is retained as base (F1 0.605, BalAcc 67.4%); inner-OOF tuned threshold 0.35 is available if higher sensitivity (79.4%) is prioritized."
